── 1b. negative control on the deployed bytes ────────────────────────────────

The equality above is only interesting if the unit is actually read. Same digits, unit
switched to pt — 7.62/10.16/15.24/20.32 typed with unit=pt:

  panel: writes 7.6/10.2/15.2/20.3 pt,  keeps 470 × 947 pt   (the mm run kept 414 × 905)
  /CropBox sheet 1: [38.3, 39.2, 507.8, 986.4]   vs mm [75.6, 67.2, 489.2, 972.4]

37.3 pt apart on the first corner. The unit moves the file; the control is not
decoration, and the four-unit agreement is not a tautology.

── 1c. red-without-fix count ─────────────────────────────────────────────────

`marginPoints` mutated to ignore its unit argument (the pre-fix behaviour: geometry
pinned to points), then `npx vitest run tests/pdf/crop-units.test.ts`:

  Tests  3 failed | 2 passed (5)     # crop-units alone
  Tests  3 failed | 121 passed (124) # across the five named files

The three that go red are the byte equality, the panel's predicted-points line, and the
panel's mm run. Unmutated: 5 passed / 124 passed. Source and the written evidence PDFs
were restored from git afterwards.

Caveat found while doing this: `tests/pdf/crop-units.test.ts` writes
`docs/research/crop-units-*.pdf` on every run, so a mutated run dirties the committed
evidence files. They differ run to run only in compressed-stream length (creation
date / file ID), never in a box; re-run the file unmutated before committing.

── 2. the retired `redact` id, and the count the UI prints ───────────────────

  #/tool/redact on the deployed site -> location.hash "#/tool/redact-pdf"
  after uploading a PDF: "Permanent redaction" panel present,
  #tool-process-btn reads "Apply 0 Redactions"

So the bookmark lands on the tool that owns the job and mounts a panel that can run it.
`getPdfTool('redact')` is undefined in this tree (pinned by field-reach.test.ts), and
`redact-pdf` declares its own `outputSuffix: '_redacted.pdf'`, so the download name does
not depend on the retired id. `src/lib/utils/download.ts` still carries a `case 'redact'`
in the legacy `ToolId` switch — a different namespace from the PDF catalogue, left alone.

Catalogue count versus what the page actually prints:

  TOOL_CATALOGUE.length = 121     PDF_TOOLS.length = 123 (2 folded ids)
  PDF_TOOL_COUNT                = 121
  deployed #/pdf headline       = "121 tools that run on your own computer"
  deployed button[data-tool]    = 121 cards

The number a visitor is told, the number of cards under it, and the catalogue agree.

